[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585255734","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3585255734","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3585255734,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Vsqk2","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T11:01:39Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T11:01:39Z","body":"While I do love this feature, I also know I am going to disable it because it clutters the script editor far too much.\r\nIt has been hugely requested, though, so let's absolutely not dismiss it. This feature is exceedingly useful for beginners and people reading code in general, but developers _should_ be aware that are huge lists of function parameters are overall bad practice. Our current API [is guilty of this](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_canvasitem.html#class-canvasitem-method-draw-string) due to general limitations, but it's usually mitigated by the use of a consistent order and proper enum constants.\r\n\r\nBe them a few personal requests: I think we would benefit from an easily accessible way to toggle these inline hints from the Script Editor itself. Say, a \"Reading or Writing\" mode of sorts.\r\nWe _could_ also enable inline hints by default, but only for boolean parameters. If you think about it, boolean parameters are the most incomprehensible of all when reading code. What does `add_child(node, true)` do at a glance?. \r\nThat, or inline hints based on a threshold of parameter numbers, which would be oddly arbitrary.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585255734/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585280784","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3585280784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3585280784,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VswsQ","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T11:08:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T11:08:41Z","body":"As an aside, i have inline parameter names enabled in every IDE that supports it. I wouldn't say it clutters the editor.\nThat being said, it definitely needs to be toggleable, and there could also be potential for configurability.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585280784/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585369002","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3585369002","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3585369002,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VtGOq","user":{"login":"Mickeon","id":66727710,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T11:31:10Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T11:31:10Z","body":"They're most definitely a controversial feature, as discussed in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110920 .\r\n\r\nI find interesting that, as I predicted, ever since the inline color picker we opened the door for other inline features, which is really cool. Perhaps we need to standardize them before proceeding further, though.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585369002/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585429033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3585429033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3585429033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VtU4p","user":{"login":"Nolkaloid","id":30960698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTYwNjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30960698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid","html_url":"https://github.com/Nolkaloid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T11:46:49Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T11:48:48Z","body":"I definitely agree with the fact that it should be standardized.\n\nIn that sense, I moved the GDScript agnostic code of the color inline color to `CodeEdit` which should IMO implement all the inline hint features that could be common to different languages.\n\nThe `CodeEdit` can then delegate the handling of the actual code action to something else, like for the Color, that is handled by the `ScriptEditor` (but we could decouple that).\n\nIdeally we would allow the delegation of more actions like delegating the click, the hover etc.\n\nOn top of that, given the fact that the hint are handled in `CodeEdit`, projects using the node could also benefit from it.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585429033/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585932838","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3585932838","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3585932838,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VvP4m","user":{"login":"JekSun97","id":130399274,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8W8Kg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130399274?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97","html_url":"https://github.com/JekSun97","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JekSun97/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T13:41:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T13:44:53Z","body":"> While I do love this feature, I also know I am going to disable it because it clutters the script editor far too much.\r\n\r\nI agree. For example, in PyCharm, this is enabled by default, and in Visual Studio, it's disabled, but I don't think it should be enable by default. Perhaps in the future, we could add a dialog box prompting the user to select code editor add-ons when they first launch Godot, so that the code editing interface better matches the user's chosen IDE.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3585932838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586984846","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3586984846","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3586984846,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VzQuO","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T18:23:45Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T18:23:45Z","body":"Would it be possible to use the same structure for the API in `ScriptLanguage` that is utilized by the language server protocol: https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#textDocument_inlayHint ? It would be nice if new features in the script editor would be developed with that in mind to reduce the amount of glue code needed to get stuff working with the language server.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3586984846/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587008897","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3587008897","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3587008897,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VzWmB","user":{"login":"Nolkaloid","id":30960698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwOTYwNjk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30960698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid","html_url":"https://github.com/Nolkaloid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nolkaloid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T18:38:19Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T18:39:58Z","body":"That's a good point, and I actually hesitated to add LSP support in the PR.\r\nIf I understand what you suggest, each inline info  `Dictionary`  should match  this structure: https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/#inlayHint (or at least the none optional ones) ?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587008897/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587078992","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3587078992","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3587078992,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VzntQ","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T19:17:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T19:17:04Z","body":"I don't really know why we are using dictionaries over structs here in the first place. And specifically the glue of converting structs to dicts seems absolutely fine to me. It's easy to generate when the structure matches.\r\n\r\nAnyway I don't think it's necessary to fully match. Like if we don't want to support certain stuff because it's very complicated leaving it away is fine.\r\n\r\nBut if it's easy to extract and is present in LSP I believe it's worth adding (e.g. `kind`). And if it's relevant for both, following the LSP structure makes sense (e.g. `position`).\r\n\r\nIn addition I'm also talking about the input params. LSP allows specifying a range for which to calculate hints. It would be nice to add this to our API. If CodeEdit does not support it, we can simply pass the whole document range. But it allows us to optimize the internal GDScript implementation for more advanced external editors (e.g. by stop visiting nodes once the end of the node is past the provided range).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587078992/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3890034698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113214#issuecomment-3890034698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113214","id":3890034698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7n3TgK","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravat